Sergiu Gatlan has an update on a case previously noted on this site. A former core infrastructure engineer at an industrial company headquartered in New Jersey was sentenced to 32 months in prison for locking thousands of devices on his employer&#8217;s network in a ransomware-style attack. 57-year-old Daniel Rhyne from Kansas City, Missouri, pleaded guilty...
<p><a href="https://databreaches.net/2026/10/06/engineer-sentenced-for-locking-over-3000-devices-on-employers-network/">Source</a></p>

